Finding a lojbanic name has never really been of interest to me. It's  
like technically my name(Zachary) means "God's Chosen" or something  
of the sort, but I'm never really cared that much. To me a name is an  
otherwise nonsensical label. Mixing names and words in English can be  
very confusing.
Example:
Man 1: Man, can you believe that Big Tree?
Man 2: What tree? I don't see any trees.
Man 1:No, no, Big Tree. The Person.
Man 2:Ohhh...

Then again, that's not so much of a problem in Lojban because of la.

With that malglico little rant out of the way, allow me to vote for  
la vesysev. Not only is it palindromic, it is also somewhat lyric and  
pleasing to both the ears and the tongue.

mi'e la ZAkyris.
